ing=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">How do screen rooms stay cool in Florida heat?</h3></div><nav class=\"dropdown-list w-dropdown-list\"><p class=\"grey\">Screen room installations allow natural airflow while blocking direct sun, helping patios stay up to 15 degrees cooler in Florida heat. Aluminum frames and fine mesh screens work together to reduce solar heat gain, improve comfort, and extend the usable hours of your outdoor living space.</p></nav></div><div data-delay=\"0\" data-hover=\"false\" data-w-id=\"9f159d33-eb67-9087-202c-bab1e4077bcf\" class=\"dropdown-faq w-dropdown\"><div class=\"dropdown-toggle w-dropdown-toggle\"><div class=\"block-arrow-faq\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/open-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-open\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">Are screen rooms storm-rated for Florida weather?</h3></div><nav class=\"dropdown-list w-dropdown-list\"><p class=\"grey\">Screen rooms are built with rust-resistant, powder-coated aluminum frames and reinforced mesh to meet Florida's hurricane and wind-load building codes. As licensed contractors, Rob and Val at Mr. &amp; Mrs. Outdoor Living manage all permitting and inspections, ensuring every installation is structurally certified and code-compliant.</p></nav></div><div data-delay=\"0\" data-hover=\"false\" data-w-id=\"9f159d33-eb67-9087-202c-bab1e4077bd7\" class=\"dropdown-faq w-dropdown\"><div class=\"dropdown-toggle w-dropdown-toggle\"><div class=\"block-arrow-faq\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/open-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-open\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">Do screen rooms keep out mosquitoes in South Florida?</h3></div><nav class=\"dropdown-list w-dropdown-list\"><p class=\"grey\">Yes. Custom patio screen rooms use fine aluminum mesh rated to block mosquitoes, no-see-ums, and other insects common in South Florida. The mesh maintains consistent airflow while creating a comfortable, insect-free living environment. Homeowners can upgrade to pet-resistant or solar-shade mesh for additional durability and UV protection.</p></nav></div><div data-delay=\"0\" data-hover=\"false\" data-w-id=\"9f159d33-eb67-9087-202c-bab1e4077bdf\" class=\"dropdown-faq w-dropdown\"><div class=\"dropdown-toggle w-dropdown-toggle\"><div class=\"block-arrow-faq\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/open-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-open\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">How long do patio screen rooms last in Florida?</h3></div><nav class=\"dropdown-list w-dropdown-list\"><p class=\"grey\">High-quality aluminum-frame screen rooms last 20 to 30 years or more in Florida's coastal climate. Powder-coated frames resist rust and UV degradation, while quality mesh materials maintain integrity without frequent replacement. Routine rinsing and periodic door hardware inspections are all that's needed to preserve long-term performance.</p></nav></div><div data-delay=\"0\" data-hover=\"false\" data-w-id=\"9f159d33-eb67-9087-202c-bab1e4077be7\" class=\"dropdown-faq w-dropdown\"><div class=\"dropdown-toggle w-dropdown-toggle\"><div class=\"block-arrow-faq\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/open-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-open\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">Can I fully customize my outdoor project design?</h3></div><nav class=\"dropdown-list w-dropdown-list\"><p class=\"grey\">Choose from clear-view screens, pet-resistant mesh, solar-shade panels, kick plates, integrated lighting, and ceiling fans to personalize your 